&lt;h3&gt;


The Build with React Image Editor Challenge
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Shared by &lt;strong&gt;Konark Sharma (&lt;a class="mentioned-user" href="https://dev.to/konark_13"&gt;@konark_13&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Konark shared the &lt;strong&gt;Build with React Image Editor Challenge&lt;/strong&gt; from &lt;strong&gt;Unlayer&lt;/strong&gt;, where you build a GTA VI-inspired experience using &lt;strong&gt;React Image Editor&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The idea is to build something where users can edit or customize at least one visual, use React Image Editor as a core part of the project, and then publish the source code in a public GitHub repository and deploy the project.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I wanted to include this because it's a little different from the usual hackathons I come across. The GTA VI theme gives you a starting point, but there is still quite a bit of room for what you can actually build around it.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;There is &lt;strong&gt;$1,000 in prizes&lt;/strong&gt;, with $500 for first place, $300 for second, and $200 for third. Projects are judged on creativity, visual execution, use of React Image Editor, and the overall experience.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Format:&lt;/strong&gt; Online&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deadline:&lt;/strong&gt; September 24, 2026 at 11:59 PM UTC&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Prize Pool:&lt;/strong&gt; $1,000&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you need to build:&lt;/strong&gt; A GTA VI-inspired experience using React Image Editor, with at least one visual that users can edit or customize.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Submission:&lt;/strong&gt; Public GitHub repository + deployed project&lt;/p&gt;

