&lt;p&gt;Compliance with Facebook policies&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Account age should not replace these fundamentals.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Businesses should focus on building sustainable audiences rather than depending entirely on the age of an account.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Facebook Profiles vs. Facebook Pages&lt;br&gt;
It is also important to distinguish between a Facebook profile and a Facebook Page.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Personal Profile&lt;br&gt;
A profile is generally associated with an individual and personal social activity.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Facebook Page&lt;br&gt;
A Page can represent:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A business&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Organization&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Creator&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Brand&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Public figure&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Community&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Businesses that want to build a long-term brand presence should consider whether a Page is more appropriate than relying on a personal profile.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Choosing the correct Facebook product can make account management more organized and sustainable.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Old Accounts and Facebook Advertising&lt;br&gt;
Another reason people may search for old Facebook accounts is advertising.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;However, an old account should not be considered a guaranteed shortcut to advertising approval or performance.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Advertising systems can involve separate requirements, review processes, payment information, business information, and policy compliance.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;An older personal profile does not automatically guarantee:&lt;/p&gt;

