&lt;p&gt;Frequently Asked Questions&lt;br&gt;
What is an old Facebook account?&lt;br&gt;
An old Facebook account is generally a profile that has existed for a relatively long period. The exact age can vary depending on the account.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Does an old Facebook account automatically have better reach?&lt;br&gt;
No. Account age alone does not guarantee better organic reach, engagement, advertising performance, or visibility.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Is an old Facebook account automatically trusted?&lt;br&gt;
No. Account age should not be treated as a guarantee of trust or unrestricted access.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Can an old Facebook account still be restricted?&lt;br&gt;
Yes. Older accounts can still encounter security checks, temporary restrictions, or enforcement actions depending on activity and circumstances.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;What should I check before using an established Facebook account?&lt;br&gt;
Consider account history, security, recovery options, privacy settings, connected applications, login sessions, and compliance with Facebook's rules.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Is account age the same as account quality?&lt;br&gt;
No. Age is only one characteristic. Account quality involves broader factors such as security, legitimate activity, content history, and policy compliance.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Can an old account guarantee Facebook advertising approval?&lt;br&gt;
No. Advertising approval depends on applicable requirements and review processes. Account age alone does not guarantee approval.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;How can I improve Facebook account security?&lt;br&gt;
Use a unique password, enable available two-factor authentication, secure your email, review login sessions, and monitor security notifications.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Why should I review old posts?&lt;br&gt;
Old posts may contain outdated personal information, photographs, opinions, or public content that no longer represents your current preferences.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Is a purchased old Facebook account risk-free?&lt;br&gt;
No. Account history, ownership, security, recovery, and platform-policy issues can create uncertainty.&lt;/p&gt;

